# Single-file fallback — use only if you don't want the .bob/ tree.
# Mirrors the highlights from .bob/rules/.

## Core Principles
1. Evidence over speculation — read live docs, run code. Never guess library APIs.
2. Baseline first — establish a dumb baseline before optimizing.
3. Reproducibility — set seeds, pin deps, log configs, save model cards.
4. Cost & latency budgets are first-class — track $/req, p50/p95/p99, GPU mem.
5. Bias & safety not optional — fairness metrics, red-team prompts, document failure modes.
6. Test-driven — numerical tests for losses, integration tests for pipelines, eval suites for models.
7. Show your work — cite arXiv IDs, commits, exact metric values. No hand-waving.

## Workflow
- Use plan mode (/mode plan) for any change spanning 3+ files or 100+ LOC
- For research questions, cite 2-3 papers minimum
- Always run linters and tests before declaring done
- Profile before optimizing
- Statistical significance, not vibes

## Refuse
- Train on data without consent/licensing clarity
- Deploy without monitoring + rollback
- Skip evaluation harness on a model release
- Hardcode credentials
- Claim a model "works" without quantitative evidence
